<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean crop 40 pct harvested - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean crop 40 pct harvested - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 40 percent of Brazil's expected soybean crop had been harvested by March 27, consultants Safras e Mercado said in a weekly report.</p>
<p>The 40 percent compares with 30 percent by March 28, 1996, and an historical average over the past five years of 27 percent, it added.  </p>
<p>The main worry at the moment is the dry weather in Rio Grande do Sul where there has been no significant rainfall since the end of February.</p>
<p>Rains during the previous weekend were very light and irregular and did not resolve any humidity problems.</p>
<p>There is so far no concrete figure for losses but there is no doubt that the current forecast of 5.9 million tonnes will be affected, Safras said.</p>
<p>A breakdown of percentage harvested by state follows:  </p>
<p> STATE		     27/03/97   20/03/97   28/03/96  5-yr avge</p>
<p> Rio Grande do Sul	  6	     1	    2	   3</p>
<p> Parana			63	    45	   46	  50</p>
<p> Mato Grosso		 54	    48	   40	  35</p>
<p> Mato Grosso do Sul	49	    39	   40	  38</p>
<p> Goias			 52	    40	   42	  28</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		   80	    60	   78	  67</p>
<p> Minas Gerais		30	    20	   14	  16</p>
<p> Others			12	     7	   10	   6</p>
<p> TOTAL BRAZIL		40	    30	   30	  27</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
